.TH CHARDETECT "1" "February 2026" "" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
.B chardetect
\(en takes one or more file paths and reports their detected encodings
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B chardetect
.RB [ \-h ]
.RB [ \-\-minimal ]
.RB [ \-l ]
.RB [ \-e\ \fIENCODING_ERA ]
.RB [ \-\-version ]
.RI [ input \ ...]
.SH OPTIONS
.SS "POSITIONAL ARGUMENTS"
.TP
.I input
File whose encoding we would like to determine.
(default:
.IR stdin )
.SS "OPTIONAL ARGUMENTS"
.TP
.B \-h\fR, \fB\-\-help
Show a help message and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-minimal
Print only the encoding to standard output.
.TP
.B \-l\fR, \fB\-\-legacy
Rename legacy encodings to more modern ones.
.TP
.B \-e\fR, \fB\-\-encoding\-era\ \fIENCODING_ERA
Which era of encodings to consider
(default:
.BR MODERN_WEB ).
Choices:
.BR MODERN_WEB ,
.BR LEGACY_ISO ,
.BR LEGACY_MAC ,
.BR LEGACY_REGIONAL ,
.BR DOS ,
.BR MAINFRAME ,
.BR ALL
.TP
.B \-\-version
Show program\(cqs version number and exit.
